IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `scja-core`
IMPORT `scja3-sch10-tenth-schedule`

-- scja3-tests-sch10.l4: tests for the Tenth Schedule.  Expected values are written from the text of the Schedule
-- (SCJA1969.txt lines 6542-6584) beside each assertion, and not from the module's output.

§ `Tests: the Tenth Schedule`

`sch 10 test: no consent` MEANS `sch 10 facts about the consents` OF FALSE, FALSE
`sch 10 test: each party consents to the relief sought` MEANS `sch 10 facts about the consents` OF TRUE, FALSE
`sch 10 test: every party consents to the withdrawal` MEANS `sch 10 facts about the consents` OF FALSE, TRUE
`sch 10 test: both consents` MEANS `sch 10 facts about the consents` OF TRUE, TRUE

-- ---- the limbs ----
#ASSERT (`sch 10 para 1(a) the matter is an application for permission to apply to review an earlier decision` `sch 10 an application under section 394H of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 for permission to apply to the Court of Appeal to review an earlier decision of the Court of Appeal`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 10 para 1(a) the matter is an application for permission to apply to review an earlier decision` `sch 10 another matter`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 10 para 1(b) the matter is a criminal motion for which each party consents to the relief or remedy sought` `sch 10 a criminal motion mentioned in section 408A of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010` `sch 10 test: each party consents to the relief sought`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a section 408A motion without the consent of each party
#ASSERT (`sch 10 para 1(b) the matter is a criminal motion for which each party consents to the relief or remedy sought` `sch 10 a criminal motion mentioned in section 408A of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010` `sch 10 test: no consent`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- consent to a withdrawal is not consent to the relief sought in the motion
#ASSERT (`sch 10 para 1(b) the matter is a criminal motion for which each party consents to the relief or remedy sought` `sch 10 a criminal motion mentioned in section 408A of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010` `sch 10 test: every party consents to the withdrawal`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 10 para 1(b) the matter is a criminal motion for which each party consents to the relief or remedy sought` `sch 10 another matter` `sch 10 test: both consents`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 10 para 2(a) the matter is an order summarily giving permission to withdraw an appeal where every party consents` `sch 10 an order under section 378(5A) of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 summarily giving permission to withdraw an appeal` `sch 10 test: every party consents to the withdrawal`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 10 para 2(a) the matter is an order summarily giving permission to withdraw an appeal where every party consents` `sch 10 an order under section 378(5A) of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 summarily giving permission to withdraw an appeal` `sch 10 test: each party consents to the relief sought`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 10 para 2(a) the matter is an order summarily giving permission to withdraw an appeal where every party consents` `sch 10 an order under section 408A(4) of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 summarily giving permission to withdraw a criminal motion` `sch 10 test: every party consents to the withdrawal`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 10 para 2(b) the matter is an order summarily giving permission to withdraw a criminal motion where every party consents` `sch 10 an order under section 408A(4) of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 summarily giving permission to withdraw a criminal motion` `sch 10 test: every party consents to the withdrawal`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 10 para 2(b) the matter is an order summarily giving permission to withdraw a criminal motion where every party consents` `sch 10 an order under section 408A(4) of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 summarily giving permission to withdraw a criminal motion` `sch 10 test: no consent`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 10 para 2(b) the matter is an order summarily giving permission to withdraw a criminal motion where every party consents` `sch 10 an order under section 378(5A) of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 summarily giving permission to withdraw an appeal` `sch 10 test: every party consents to the withdrawal`) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---- seam 16: the smaller panel the Tenth Schedule allows ----
#ASSERT (`sch 10 the smaller panel the Tenth Schedule allows` `Court of Appeal` `sch 10 an application under section 394H of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 for permission to apply to the Court of Appeal to review an earlier decision of the Court of Appeal` `sch 10 test: no consent`) EQUALS JUST `a single Judge`
#ASSERT (`sch 10 the smaller panel the Tenth Schedule allows` `Court of Appeal` `sch 10 a criminal motion mentioned in section 408A of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010` `sch 10 test: each party consents to the relief sought`) EQUALS JUST `a single Judge`
#ASSERT (`sch 10 the smaller panel the Tenth Schedule allows` `Court of Appeal` `sch 10 an order under section 378(5A) of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 summarily giving permission to withdraw an appeal` `sch 10 test: every party consents to the withdrawal`) EQUALS JUST `a single Judge`
#ASSERT (`sch 10 the smaller panel the Tenth Schedule allows` `Court of Appeal` `sch 10 an order under section 408A(4) of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 summarily giving permission to withdraw a criminal motion` `sch 10 test: every party consents to the withdrawal`) EQUALS JUST `a single Judge`
-- listed, but the consent the Schedule asks for is missing: the Schedule does not provide a single Judge
#ASSERT (`sch 10 the smaller panel the Tenth Schedule allows` `Court of Appeal` `sch 10 a criminal motion mentioned in section 408A of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010` `sch 10 test: no consent`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`sch 10 the smaller panel the Tenth Schedule allows` `Court of Appeal` `sch 10 another matter` `sch 10 test: both consents`) EQUALS NOTHING
-- any other court: the Schedule does not speak of it
#ASSERT (`sch 10 the smaller panel the Tenth Schedule allows` `Appellate Division` `sch 10 an application under section 394H of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 for permission to apply to the Court of Appeal to review an earlier decision of the Court of Appeal` `sch 10 test: no consent`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`sch 10 the smaller panel the Tenth Schedule allows` `General Division` `sch 10 a criminal motion mentioned in section 408A of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010` `sch 10 test: both consents`) EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- the yes/no twin ----
#ASSERT (`sch 10 the Tenth Schedule allows a single Judge` `Court of Appeal` `sch 10 a criminal motion mentioned in section 408A of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010` `sch 10 test: each party consents to the relief sought`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 10 the Tenth Schedule allows a single Judge` `Court of Appeal` `sch 10 a criminal motion mentioned in section 408A of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010` `sch 10 test: no consent`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 10 the Tenth Schedule allows a single Judge` `Court of Appeal` `sch 10 another matter` `sch 10 test: both consents`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 10 the Tenth Schedule allows a single Judge` `Appellate Division` `sch 10 a criminal motion mentioned in section 408A of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010` `sch 10 test: each party consents to the relief sought`) EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT (`sch 10 the limbs taken together` (LIST JUST FALSE, JUST TRUE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 10 the limbs taken together` (LIST JUST FALSE, JUST FALSE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 10 the limbs taken together` (LIST JUST FALSE, NOTHING)) EQUALS NOTHING
